#' Example data for restricted win statistics
#'
#' A simulated two-component prioritized survival data set for illustrating
#' restricted win statistics with right censoring. The data are stored in
#' long format. Each subject has one follow-up/censoring row with
#' `event_type = 0`; subjects with observed component events before the
#' restriction time have additional event rows with `event_type = 1` or
#' `event_type = 2`.
#'
#' @format A data frame with columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{id}{Subject identifier.}
#'   \item{A}{Treatment arm indicator; `1` for treatment and `0` for control.}
#'   \item{Z1}{Binary baseline covariate.}
#'   \item{Z2}{Continuous baseline covariate.}
#'   \item{Z3}{Binary baseline covariate.}
#'   \item{event_type}{Endpoint type. `0` is the follow-up/censoring row,
#'     `1` is the first-priority endpoint, and `2` is the second-priority endpoint.}
#'   \item{priority}{Endpoint priority order; `0` for the follow-up/censoring row.}
#'   \item{label}{Text label for the endpoint type.}
#'   \item{time}{Observed row-specific time used in `Surv(time, status)`.}
#'   \item{status}{Row-specific event indicator. For event rows, `1` indicates
#'     that the endpoint event was observed. For the follow-up row, `1` indicates
#'     censoring before the restriction time.}
#'   \item{tau}{Restriction time used to construct the observed data.}
#' }
#'
#' @details
#' The data were simulated from Weibull proportional hazards margins linked by
#' a Gumbel--Hougaard dependence structure, with covariate-dependent censoring.
#' The object is intended only as a reproducible example for the package API.
#'
#' @source Simulated using `data-raw/windat.R` from the package source tree.
#'
#' @examples
#' data(windat)
#' head(windat)
#'
#' \dontrun{
#' fit <- winIPCW(
#'   survival::Surv(time, status) ~ Z1 + Z2 + Z3,
#'   data = windat,
#'   id = "id",
#'   trt = "A",
#'   endpoint = "event_type",
#'   tau = c(12, 24, 36),
#'   method = c("ipcw", "m-ipcw"),
#'   estimand = c("NB", "WR", "WO"),
#'   priority = c(1, 2),
#'   censor = "cox",
#'   margin = "cox",
#'   copula = "gumbel"
#' )
#' summary(fit)
#' }
"windat"
